            <ArticleTitle>Omalizumab for severe allergic asthma: 7 years and open questions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>158-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1159/000360771</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anti-IgE treatment for severe allergic asthma has been available for more than seven years now. This treatment has clear clinical benefits and a good safety record. However, important questions concerning long-term dosing and treatment duration remain unanswered. This paper discusses the available information concerning the long-term use of omalizumab.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
